---
import { links, requirement, trustLine } from "../content/site";

/** Tone examples from the brand's personality.md: how a Night's verdict reads. */
const verdicts = [
	"Night done. 2 pull requests open.",
	"Night done. Nothing was ready.",
	"Blocked: check failure. Answer it in Linear, not here.",
];
---

<section aria-labelledby="hero-heading" class="hero-fade">
	<div class="grid lg:grid-cols-12">
		<div class="px-4 pt-14 pb-12 sm:px-8 sm:pt-20 lg:col-span-7 lg:pt-24 lg:pb-20">
			<p class="flex items-center gap-3">
				<img
					src="/yellowhammer-mark.svg"
					alt=""
					width="40"
					height="40"
					class="size-10"
				/>
				<span class="text-xl font-bold tracking-tight">Yellowhammer</span>
				<span class="ledger-label ml-1 border-l border-rule pl-3">For Mac</span>
			</p>
			<h1
				id="hero-heading"
				class="mt-8 text-[2.5rem] leading-[1.05] font-bold tracking-tight text-balance sm:text-6xl"
			>
				Wake up to <span class="highlight">pull requests</span>.
			</h1>
			<p class="mt-4 text-xl leading-snug font-medium text-balance text-ink sm:text-2xl">
				Yellowhammer picked the work from your spec.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-6 max-w-[56ch] text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
				Yellowhammer runs an unattended engineering Shift on top of Orca ADE: one Night for
				each of your Projects, all of them at once. It takes intent from your Linear board,
				hands the work to your agent CLIs, and opens one pull request per repository by
				morning.
			</p>
			<div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
				<a href={links.download} class="button-primary h-11 px-5 text-base">Download for Mac</a>
				<a href={links.repo} class="button-secondary h-11 px-5 text-base">View on GitHub</a>
			</div>
			<p class="mt-4 text-sm text-ink-muted">
				<span class="font-semibold text-ink">{requirement}.</span>{" "}
				{trustLine}
			</p>
		</div>
		<aside
			aria-labelledby="verdicts-heading"
			class="border-t border-rule px-4 py-10 sm:px-8 lg:col-span-5 lg:border-t-0 lg:border-l lg:py-24"
		>
			<h2 id="verdicts-heading" class="ledger-label">Every Night ends with a verdict</h2>
			<p class="mt-3 max-w-[40ch] text-ink-muted">
				The Night Summary leads with the outcome, then the reason. These lines show the
				tone; they are examples, not a record.
			</p>
			<ol class="mt-6 border-t border-rule">
				{
					verdicts.map((line, index) => (
						<li class="flex gap-4 border-b border-rule py-4">
							<span class="ledger-label pt-0.5" aria-hidden="true">
								{String(index + 1).padStart(2, "0")}
							</span>
							<span class="font-mono text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed">{line}</span>
						</li>
					))
				}
			</ol>
			<p class="mt-6 text-sm text-ink-muted">
				An empty Night and a crashed Night each say what they were. You never open a
				terminal to find out.
			</p>
		</aside>
	</div>
</section>
